---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Contact | defamationcalc.com';
const description = 'Contact the defamationcalc.com editorial team with corrections, feedback, or questions about defamation law content.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Contact defamationcalc.com</h1>
  <p>The best way to reach us is by email at <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. We read every message and respond to substantive corrections and editorial feedback within five business days.</p>

  <h2>What We Can Help With</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Factual corrections:</strong> If you have identified an error in a case citation, a doctrine we have misstated, or a damages figure that is inconsistent with published verdict research, we want to know. Include the specific claim, the page URL, and your source.</li>
    <li><strong>Methodology questions:</strong> If you have questions about how the calculator produces its estimates — the baselines, the multipliers, the range logic — we are happy to explain. The <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> documents the full framework, but we can answer follow-up questions.</li>
    <li><strong>Content feedback:</strong> If a topic in defamation law is missing from the guides or FAQ, or if existing content is unclear or poorly organized, we welcome that feedback.</li>
    <li><strong>Editorial policy:</strong> Questions about our corrections policy, editorial standards, or how content is reviewed are always welcome.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What We Cannot Help With</h2>
  <p>We are not a law firm and cannot provide legal advice or case-specific analysis. We do not respond to requests such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>"Do I have a defamation case?"</li>
    <li>"How much is my specific defamation claim worth?"</li>
    <li>"Can you review my situation and tell me what to do?"</li>
    <li>"Can you recommend a defamation attorney?"</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For case-specific guidance, consult a licensed defamation attorney in your jurisdiction. Many defamation attorneys offer initial consultations, and state bar associations maintain referral directories.</p>

  <h2>Media and Press Inquiries</h2>
  <p>If you are writing about defamation law and would like to reference our calculator methodology or editorial content, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with your publication and the nature of the inquiry. We respond to press inquiries within two business days.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>defamationcalc.com is monetized exclusively through Google AdSense display advertising. We do not accept sponsored content, paid placements, or advertising arrangements outside the AdSense platform. Advertising-related inquiries will not receive a response.</p>

  <p>Return to the <a href="/">calculator</a> or see the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
